<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH BREWER PRAZDROJ POSTS LOWER '96 NET.</title>
<headline>CZECH BREWER PRAZDROJ POSTS LOWER '96 NET.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Plzen-based Czech brewer Plzensky Prazdroj a.s. said on Wednesday its audited 1996 results showed a net profit of 74.9 million crowns down from 158.061 million crowns a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The amount of profit was influenced by the investment into construction which last year totalled about 1.2 billion crowns, Prazdroj spokesman Jaroslav Pomp told Reuters.  </p>
<p>				     1996		 1995</p>
<p> net profit (czk mln)	 74.926    vs     158.061</p>
<p> gross profit		   90.122	     183.165</p>
<p> operating profit	    400.390	     531.846</p>
<p> writeoffs		     591.060	     444.832</p>
<p> total turnover	    3,963.203	   3,129.080</p>
<p> sales of external goods   710.282	     590.452</p>
<p>sales of own products</p>
<p> and services		3,672.520	   2,974.431</p>
<p> income from investment    172.281		67.545</p>
<p> basic capital	     1,939.020	   1,939.020</p>
<p> total assets		6,519.913	   5,337.406</p>
<p> current assets	    1,631.074	   1,243.143</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Plzensky Prazdroj a.s., makers</p>
<p>of Pilsner Urquell and Gambrinus lagers, among others.</p>
<p>The company has forecast its 1997 net profit at 125 million</p>
<p>crowns on total sales of 6.6 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The largest shareholders are, according to filings with the</p>
<p>Central Securities Registry in March, IPB a.s. with 18</p>
<p>percent, RIF Fund with 18 percent, and the Czech</p>
<p>state National Property Fund with 17 percent.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
